    {
      "title": "Facts and statements",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Google’s September 2022 encryption matrix explicitly lists MongoDB Atlas with Cloud KMS and CloudHSM support. MongoDB’s shared responsibility model also includes HSM-backed customer-managed keys. (high confidence) (verified as of 2022-09-16) Sources: https://mongodb.com/resources/products/fundamentals/shared-responsibility",
          "source": "https://mongodb.com/resources/products/fundamentals/shared-responsibility",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:b13225f66cc269e907ff0129773b64db28257d4872f4b55ae6a3c66adad3e978",
          "validationStatus": "REMEDIATED-PROJECTION",
          "evidenceIds": [],
          "also": [
            "https://www.mongodb.com/resources/products/fundamentals/shared-responsibility",
            "https://cloud.google.com/kms/docs/hsm"
          ],
          "originValidationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "originEvidenceIds": [
            "ev:115502c9a32bb64ef5d04a929434521908d3db7d89198d1177ef91ac74e8abf8",
            "ev:53d760216a4de1cee744221ec2f95ed3cbfa19a25a003aa825355e8232024bfa",
            "ev:fccc25c0b101771252034bbc62bb916a6d0f4b6c4e97dc0c0c30062ac324bef9"
          ],
          "remediation": {
            "schema": "claim-remediation-projection/v1",
            "record": "remediation.json",
            "requires_revalidation": true,
            "claim_text_sha256": "1f90cef970547b3da66273cfe854748d34984136dfa986ddfd9471f19e86557d"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Cloud HSM exposes hardware-backed cryptographic operations through Cloud KMS. Google manages the HSM cluster, including scaling and patching. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://cloud.google.com/kms/docs/hsm",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:3d4ba80d5fbdb3d36bb3d8a0caf90aad754ebed18a21d446315d15c79b3fbba7",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:113c8d089eb1628c651cd4a53fce6e58aaa8bc1c13264344ea4ed06b3e3926ca"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://cloud.google.com/blog/topics/inside-google-cloud/architecting-for-database-encryption-on-google-cloud"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Atlas uses the Google Cloud customer-managed key to wrap per-node MongoDB master keys; those master keys wrap per-database encryption keys used by WiredTiger. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/security-gcp-kms.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:c8dfb70f88aab9322a1adbc136cf56cdf29c0127e4598675e0b6a2d2686d836d",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:3acce97cd5a596288c40a09f45cfaa0a2f0ac9011fd33b8459ce30b918b49902"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For the documented integration, create a symmetric encrypt/decrypt key with HSM protection in Cloud KMS, then supply its fully qualified CryptoKeyVersion resource name to Atlas and grant the Atlas identity the required key permissions. (medium confidence) Sources: https://cloud.google.com/kms/docs/hsm ; https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/security-gcp-kms.md",
          "source": "https://cloud.google.com/kms/docs/hsm",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:7e2ee76e1c4baf3b0bd828360f085348018fdb10902f565a15b2c99445e87882",
          "validationStatus": "REMEDIATED-PROJECTION",
          "evidenceIds": [],
          "also": [
            "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/security-gcp-kms.md"
          ],
          "originValidationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "originEvidenceIds": [
            "ev:036d454d75daa6b42a5de877d6d1c41391433cce655c2b8d3eba141ac69fbe81",
            "ev:2c477dc802299c2e445e350cf6c6e4c92bcdaad1e68362fc21f87d2c12792857",
            "ev:4cad6c03362d9275e87313f7de42305efbe7074cf2a932a34f0d87d13334297f",
            "ev:5538256d6680463a029cebaf7e171df6168f972f8c3ab50e990ec07811e3a1b5"
          ],
          "remediation": {
            "schema": "claim-remediation-projection/v1",
            "record": "remediation.json",
            "requires_revalidation": true,
            "claim_text_sha256": "ff0f0bed6735a1665a360223571e12af07eb43d20a407fc2a4f8a2f780b8f632"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "The Atlas Google Cloud KMS guide requires M10 or larger clusters, Project Owner access, project-level configuration, and subsequent enablement on each target cluster; Free and Flex clusters are excluded. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-14)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/security-gcp-kms.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:076853524c1c5f2b9b5deb8bde9c092edb2b27aafb5def7717659f7bfee239e5",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:2c477dc802299c2e445e350cf6c6e4c92bcdaad1e68362fc21f87d2c12792857",
            "ev:4851988e23e0223187137889b5042205808f571f79e543f8af32b813431b82b8",
            "ev:af352be08505139b56b6a1fa7a3ddda87d3773e0a08ac6ebfed246976bcb8eb6",
            "ev:f4ac5e38be832f55392188a4ea1f30f19826cddd8327bd5c289600437294317b"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Atlas does not automatically rotate its configured Google Cloud Key Version Resource ID. Update Atlas after key rotation, and retain the old version until changes deploy and no retained snapshot needs it. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-14)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/security-gcp-kms.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:a4c9264c8ffb96966db76d96c089f98410bbbd2d9a5e9fada7aaa7f368a80cf8",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:cac8eca0a84b78822f0575122dbdb34654a1a6a18ecc197046ee70a7e93b3f07"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MongoDB warns that revoking Atlas access to its customer-managed key shuts down cluster nodes and makes data inaccessible until key access is restored. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/security-gcp-kms.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:99ec0bd25945f8889c9d81c40d6da5894ef491bb128a7252ba97d4c48dda171b",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:941eacc9fac37fc0d98844cd08f6a4707d47e43db01fcbff5da3380c09cfe47c"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Treat key storage, least-privilege access, rotation, and recovery as operational responsibilities. Percona recommends dedicated KMS or HSM storage and key lifecycle controls; MongoDB assigns customer-managed key configuration and access policies to customers. (high confidence) Sources: https://www.percona.com/blog/securing-your-mongodb-database-essential-best-practices/ ; https://mongodb.com/resources/products/fundamentals/shared-responsibility",
          "source": "https://www.percona.com/blog/securing-your-mongodb-database-essential-best-practices/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:9cd1beb7da083935ba06a4012fc52a25602fa0fb6cead7c6ecc84b9565285a47",
          "validationStatus": "REMEDIATED-PROJECTION",
          "evidenceIds": [],
          "also": [
            "https://www.mongodb.com/resources/products/fundamentals/shared-responsibility",
            "https://mongodb.com/resources/products/fundamentals/shared-responsibility"
          ],
          "originValidationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "originEvidenceIds": [
            "ev:e4210d7f8f6c76c1c24548e0357bdfc699495923d40d056d579adf95be8b2653",
            "ev:fccc25c0b101771252034bbc62bb916a6d0f4b6c4e97dc0c0c30062ac324bef9"
          ],
          "remediation": {
            "schema": "claim-remediation-projection/v1",
